# Ship a complete, buildable source tree in the sdist so that
# `pip install litespark-inference` reproduces `pip install -e .` from the
# repo on ANY architecture: the per-arch SIMD kernel sources must all be
# present, because setup.py picks (and compiles) the right one on the
# *user's* machine at install time. Without this, an sdist built on (say)
# arm64 would only carry the NEON source and fail to compile on x86_64.

include LICENSE
include README.md
include pyproject.toml
include setup.py

# All SIMD kernel sources for every supported ISA (arm64 NEON, x86_64
# AVX-512 / AVX2 / VNNI fallbacks). setup.py compiles the one matching the
# install host.
recursive-include litespark_inference/kernels *.cpp *.h *.hpp
